-9. Open Orders in the app. Pass: the sale is listed. Tap it: the lines and total match. Refunds are not offered (expected for now).
+9. Open Orders in the app. Pass: the sale is listed. Tap it: the lines and total match. Refunds are tested in T124.
 10. Settings, Connections, **Forget this sign-in**. Pass: the token and location are cleared and the Check button reports a missing token.
 11. Move my data: copy from Shopify (or Pure Tillium) to Square and see what would be copied. Pass: the plan lists items, collections and customers. Run it only on a sandbox.
 
 Tell me pass or fail for each, and the exact text of any error.
+
+## T124. Square refunds (0277)
+
+Run T123 first, on the sandbox. You need a sale from that test that sold two of one tracked item.
+
+1. Open the sale under Orders and start a refund of one of the two items, back to the way it was paid. Pass: it completes with no error, and the order shows one item left to return.
+2. In Square (Dashboard, Transactions) find the payment. Pass: a refund for the right amount is on it, with your note as the reason.
+3. Check the item's stock in the app and in Square. Pass: it went up by one.
+4. Refund the other item, and this time turn off putting it back in stock if the screen offers it. Pass: the refund goes through and the stock does not change.
+5. Try to refund the same sale again. Pass: nothing is left to return, or it refuses in plain words, and Square shows no extra refund.
+6. Pay a sale half by cash and half by gift card, then refund all of it. Pass: Square shows two refunds, one against each payment.
+7. Turn airplane mode on part way through step 1 and retry. Pass: Square shows one refund, not two.
+
+Tell me pass or fail for each, and the exact text of any error. Gift cards and exchange credit are refunded against their Square payment only: Square does not put money back on the card itself.
